<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton market shut by strike over Kashmir.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton market shut by strike over Kashmir.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton market was shut on Wednesday because of an official strike against what Pakistan calls India's occupation of Moslem-majority Kashmir.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the Karachi Cotton Association's spot rates for Niab-78, K-68 and MNH-93 were steady at 2,322.50, ($57.74) 2,515 and 2,525 rupees per maund (37.32 kg) respectively.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
